{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfs4Ug2gn3fooyXS9VxGp","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"`metrics.Counter` is now thread-safe, and `tests/test_metrics.py` passes. Before the change it failed on all three runs; after, it passed on all five.\n\n**Root cause:** `incr` did an unlocked read-modify-write on `_values`, with a `time.sleep(0)` in the middle that makes the race easy to hit. `snapshot()` and the other methods read the dict with no coordination either.\n\n**The fix** (`metrics/counter.py`, the only file changed):\n- Each counter name has its own `threading.Lock`, held across the read-modify-write in `incr`. Updates to different counters don't block each other.\n- A short `_guard` lock protects the two dicts (`_values` and the per-name lock table). It is only held briefly and never while waiting on a per-name lock, so the lock order (name lock, then guard) can't deadlock.\n- `get` and `snapshot` take `_guard`. `snapshot()` still returns a plain `dict` copy.\n- `reset(name)` takes that name's lock, so it can't race an in-flight `incr`. `reset()` with no argument takes every per-name lock in sorted order before clearing, so an `incr` can't write a stale value back after the clear.\n- The API is unchanged.\n\n**Verification:**\n- `pytest tests/test_metrics.py`: 5 of 5 runs passed.\n- A separate script with 8 threads doing mixed updates on a shared counter and per-thread counters gave exact totals, confirmed `snapshot()` returns a `dict`, and confirmed `reset(name)` and `reset()` work.\n\nI didn't commit anything, since you didn't ask for a commit. Known trade-off: the per-name lock table only grows, so a name's lock stays around after `reset()`. That's a few bytes per name ever used, and removing entries safely would need more coordination than it's worth here."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":10358,"cache_read_input_tokens":49362,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":10358},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d84ddd68-372a-4ea8-8447-ed29105949dc","uuid":"fe12d73a-9f32-493d-aed1-46873c42030b","timestamp":"2026-10-09T17:30:48.287Z","request_id":"req_011Cfs4Ufk4jS5osigf5Vobz"}
